---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Awards from '@/components/Awards.astro';
import { person, record, skills } from '@/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · Tung Tran"
  description="Background, record, skills and certificates of Tung Tran (Tom), Computing Science (Honours) at UTS Sydney and quantitative trading trainee at D+A Strategies."
>
  <article class="wrap">
    <header class="doc-head doc-head--portrait">
      <div>
        <h1 class="doc-head__title reveal" style="--i: 0">About</h1>
        <p class="doc-head__lede reveal" style="--i: 1">
          Hanoi, then Sydney. Software first, then survey research, then markets. Each step taught me to distrust
          a number until I knew how it was made.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="portrait reveal" style="--i: 2">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/img/portrait-color-sm.webp 360w, /img/portrait-color.webp 680w" sizes="17rem" type="image/webp" />
          <img src="/img/portrait-color.jpg" alt="Portrait of Tung Tran" width="680" height="970" fetchpriority="high" />
        </picture>
        <figcaption>Tung (Tom) Tran</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <div class="doc">
      <p>
        I grew up in Hanoi and moved to Sydney in 2025 to study Computing Science (Honours) at UTS, majoring in AI
        and data analytics with a statistics sub-major. My route into quantitative work was indirect. I started as
        a software engineering intern at an enterprise-software firm in Hanoi, building a document Q&amp;A prototype
        and a database schema for a million-plus records. Then came survey research with collaborators in Vietnam,
        the UK and Australia, where I ran the structural-equation models and the checks that decide whether a
        finding is real. A data-analyst internship in Sydney, with returns, CAPM betas and regressions on real prices,
        is where markets stopped being an interest and became the work.
      </p>
      <p>
        What I care about is the part of research that usually gets skipped: where the data came from, whether
        the test could have seen the future, and what the result looks like after costs. My two current studies
        are built around that: <a href="/projects/vn30-futures">a VN30 futures dataset I record myself</a>, and
        <a href="/projects/spy-volatility">a volatility model whose training loss is chosen before the test</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m a quantitative trading trainee at <strong>D+A Strategies</strong>, Europe’s largest student-led quant
        trading association, working on strategy development, macro research and backtesting with students from
        Oxford, Cambridge, LSE, UCL, Imperial and Bocconi. I was a finalist in IMC Prosperity 4 (#9 in Vietnam),
        and since 2022 I’ve run Second Chance, a student group in Hanoi that has raised $10,000 for STEM teaching
        and rural schools.
      </p>

      <h2>Record</h2>
      <ul class="record">
        {record.map((r) => (
          <li>
            <span class="record__when">{r.when}</span>
            <p class="record__what">{r.what} <span class="record__where">· {r.where}</span></p>
            <p class="record__note">{r.note}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>Skills</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="spec">
          <tbody>
            {skills.map((s) => (
              <tr><th scope="row">{s.group}</th><td>{s.items}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="section wrap" id="certificates" aria-labelledby="certificates-title">
    <h2 id="certificates-title" class="section__title">Certificates</h2>
    <p class="section__intro">
      Scans of the originals; select one to open it full size. Not pictured: the UTS Academic Excellence
      International Scholarship (30% of tuition).
    </p>
    <Awards />
    <p class="awards-foot">
      The one-page version of all this is the <a href={person.cv}>CV (PDF)</a>. The quickest way to reach me is
      <a href={`mailto:${person.email}`}>{person.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
